notes:
A highly formal letter-closing phrase meaning "I state this with respect." Always paired with the opening ⟦{謹啓|きんけい}→謹啓：22309_kinkei⟧. Used in ceremonial correspondence such as wedding invitations, formal notices, and official letters.

LETTER OPENING/CLOSING PAIRS (by formality):
- {前略|ぜんりゃく} / {草々|そうそう}: informal (skipping formalities)
- ⟦{拝啓|はいけい}→拝啓：12790_haikei⟧ / ⟦{敬具|けいぐ}→敬具：12977_keigu⟧: standard formal
- ⟦{謹啓|きんけい}→謹啓：22309_kinkei⟧ / {敬白|けいはく}: highly formal

SIMILAR WORDS:
- ⟦{敬具|けいぐ}→敬具：12977_keigu⟧: sincerely — the standard formal letter closing, paired with ⟦{拝啓|はいけい}→拝啓：12790_haikei⟧; less formal than {敬白|けいはく}
- {草々|そうそう}: in haste — a casual closing paired with {前略|ぜんりゃく}
- ⟦{謹啓|きんけい}→謹啓：22309_kinkei⟧: respectfully (opening) — the corresponding opening to {敬白|けいはく}
